--- FIL-56: Read line truncates a fixed buffer, sets the error flag ---
a text called 'ledger path' is "{'the workspace'}/5trunc".
open a file for writing called 'ledger' at 'ledger path'.
Write "6ld71c0udr7kvg7g2ix119o2chn7cri2b3bk16yq00e5bgqqt3kqyfwtzk96j942tr0fs87f13qpp03jqcz2g4868mvdcz\n" to 'ledger'.
Close 'ledger'.
open a file for reading called 'ledger' at 'ledger path'.
a buffer called 'the sketchpad' is 18 bytes in size.
a boolean called 'the sketchpad found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the sketchpad found an error already pending' to true.
a boolean called 'the sketchpad line was truncated' is false.
Read line from 'ledger' into 'the sketchpad'.
On error Set 'the sketchpad line was truncated' to true.
If 'the sketchpad line was truncated' is false then, Print "ASSERT FIL-56: expected 1 got {'the sketchpad line was truncated'}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad line was truncated'.
If 'the sketchpad's size is not 18 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-56: expected 18 got {'the sketchpad's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's size.
Close 'ledger'.

--- FIL-70: is available, both directions ---
